# NOTICE

**nvcodec-blackwell** derives from [mickys/nvenc](https://github.com/mickys/nvenc) (MIT), which drives the
NVIDIA NVENC/NVDEC engines from user space and exposes them through VideoToolbox on macOS. This repository adds
Blackwell (GB20x, RTX 50) support and a faster H.264 read-out path.

- `src/`, `tools/`, `src/vt/` derive from mickys/nvenc, MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 mickys.
- `src/blocklinear.c` (Blackwell 64-byte × 16-row tile layout, banded multithreaded untiling), `src/dec.c`
  layout selection, `src/vt/vtnencvt.c` GB20x detection and the VideoToolbox property reporting are
  additions in this repository, under the same MIT licence.
- `src/vtdec.c` is the H.264 decoder plug-in here; `src/vt/nvencvt_dec.c` in the upstream tree is a
  multi-codec plug-in and is not used here.

## Runs on, but does not contain

NullMoth's NVIDIA driver for macOS (<https://github.com/nullmoth/nvidia-macos-driver>) is licensed under
PolyForm Noncommercial 1.0.0. **No code or binary from it is included in this repository.** The plug-ins
here are loaded by that driver through its documented extension points (`libnvdec_h264.dylib` next to the
driver, `NVMTL_NVENCVT` for the encoder), and `install.sh` copies them into an existing driver
installation. Running the driver at all also requires that project's own licence terms.

The video plug-ins that the driver ships are prebuilt from mickys/nvenc; this repository does not
redistribute them. `install.sh` only ever *backs up* the file it replaces.

